  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Sierra Nevada obligated $1.9B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Sierra Nevada won 38 awards so far, with an average award size of $49.5M, and obligations are down 16.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $1.9B to Sierra Nevada. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $35K to Sierra Nevada. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sierra Nevada, accounting for $1.5B in obligations. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services is the second-largest market for Sierra Nevada at $297M. Sierra Nevada also has obligations in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $114M, and in Computer Systems Design Services at $4.7M. Historical obligations for Sierra Nevada rose from $112M in FY21 to $2.2B in FY25, then are $1.9B in FY26 to date. The fiscal totals are partial because FY2026 to date values are fiscal year to date and some tables report total contract values rather than obligations. This profile highlights where Sierra Nevada is concentrated by buyer and by NAICS market.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What are Sierra Nevada's recent contracting trends?",
        "body": "Sierra Nevada obligated $1.9B in FY2026 to date, down 16.2% year over year. Sierra Nevada's award count is 38 and the average award size is $49.5M. Sierra Nevada's obligations rose from $112M in FY21 to $2.2B in FY25 before reaching $1.9B in FY26 to date. Sierra Nevada's portfolio includes both large aircraft-related awards and smaller technical and R&D awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Sierra Nevada's main buyers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.9B to Sierra Nevada, making the DoD the primary buyer. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $35K to Sierra Nevada. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sierra Nevada at $1.5B, followed by All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $297M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $114M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Sierra Nevada make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Sierra Nevada made $1.9B from federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Sierra Nevada's total for the period reflects 38 awards with an average award size of $49.5M, and obligations are down 16.2% year over year. Historical obligations for Sierra Nevada were $112M in FY21, $539M in FY22, $699M in FY23, $1.3B in FY24, and $2.2B in FY25. The FY2026 figure is fiscal year to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Sierra Nevada?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the main buyer for Sierra Nevada and obligated $1.9B. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $35K. Those two agencies represent the top buying agencies for Sierra Nevada in FY2026 to date."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Sierra Nevada sell to the government?",
      "a": "Sierra Nevada sells aircraft-related products and services and professional, technical, and systems work to the government. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest market for Sierra Nevada at $1.5B, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounts for $297M. Sierra Nevada also has obligations in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $114M and in Computer Systems Design Services at $4.7M."
    },
